- Knowledge 1: Congenital hypothyroidism is characterized by low thyroid hormone levels at birth, often due to maternal iodine deficiency.  
- Knowledge 2: Common signs and symptoms of congenital hypothyroidism include hypotonia (decreased muscle tone), macroglossia (enlarged tongue), and umbilical hernia.  
- Knowledge 3: Umbilical hernia is frequently seen in infants with congenital hypothyroidism due to the laxity of abdominal muscles.

Step 3: Reasoning Process (Subject-Predicate-Object format)  
